commit 6b2a427deb1e05ee667966024c467e9b615b6473
Author: vvondruska <vaclav@re-cinq.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 16:43:30 2026 +0200

    feat(transport): drop the send_message wire alias

    T017, decided: removed. user_message is the only wire name, which is what
    the exported types have always said - UserMessagePayload.type is the
    literal 'user_message', so a TypeScript client could never construct the
    alias anyway.

    Five documents disagreed with the types and with each other. The protocol
    spec listed the alias as accepted and then used it as the name in its own
    reconnection rule; the quick start sent it, alongside a chatId the server
    has never read; the add-a-message-type how-to reproduced the two-case
    switch, so anyone following it copied the alias forward. All six sites now
    say user_message.

    No deprecation window: nothing is published, so there were no registry
    consumers to deprecate for, and the window would only ever have been cheap
    before the first release. A client still sending it gets an error frame
    carrying INVALID_MESSAGE rather than silent acceptance.

    Two consequences worth their own lines. The switch fell to two cases,
    below re-lint/prefer-polymorphism's threshold, so its suppression became
    an unused-disable error - deleted, with ADR-006 rewritten to say the
    reasoning stands and the suppression returns with a third case. And the
    changelog had grown two Security sections under one release; they are now
    one, and the alias entry is under Removed.

    The branch floor moves down by the denominator effect T016 documented:
    205/332 before, 204/331 after, 127 uncovered either way.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
